  "source_strategy": {
    "description": "Two shared XYZ terrain surfaces connect each mountain group through common ridges, saddles, shoulders and front feet. Fixed orthographic depth projection guides visible Canvas brush contacts and independent coverage. Seven layers and ten objects reuse the existing one-frame composition; clay is a separate structural diagnostic mode.",
    "tradeoffs": "Authored heightfields are spatial hypotheses, not reconstructed closed volumes. Projection is fixed-view; no orbit camera is admitted. Dense crossed hatching and bright saddle shoulders remain artistic limitations. Helper numeric storage excludes author arrays, Canvas and browser RSS."
  },
